## Users live in memory, so create user 1 first (see users.post.endpoint.http)

## Create post (valid) - expect 201
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "text": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## Unknown author - expect 404
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 999,
    "text": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## text too short, under 30 chars (@MinLength(30)) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "text": "Too short"
}

###
## authorId as string (@IsInt) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": "1",
    "text": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## Client-sent id (forbidNonWhitelisted) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": 5,
    "authorId": 1,
    "text": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## Empty body, every required field missing - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{}
